Subject: [PATCH 5/6] geph5-app: let vpn.rs reuse the linux backend on Android

Pure cfg widening: android selects the same `linux` submodule and backend alias
as linux. Android's TUN/ioctl surface is Linux's, so this is the correct
backend, and duplicating platform.rs's linux module would be worse.

KNOWN LIMITATION, unchanged by this patch: bring_tunnel_up still fails on
Android with "Linux VPN requires a service user", because ensure_service_user()
returns None there (patch 6) and vpn.rs requires a uid/gid before calling
backend::setup. Fixing full-tunnel VPN on Android is a real piece of work, not
a cfg tweak, and is out of scope for the sync model. Proxy mode, which is what
the module's action.sh uses, does not go through this path.

Fragility: medium. Roughly a dozen cfg attributes; a large share of the file
is cfg-gated, so an upstream reorganisation that moves the attributes out of
the functions they guard will produce rejects here.
